      "@id": "https://windswept.energy/ontology/overspeed",
      "class": "FailureMode",
      "canonical_name": "",
      "definition": "The condition where the rotor speed exceeds the design limit, where centrifugal loading, bearing limits, or the speed ceiling of the transmission stops being safe. The transmission is incapable of safely governing tip speed ratio, and without sufficient resistance from torque transmission the rotor accelerates freely within the aerodynamic limits of system drag.",
      "symbol": "",
      "dimension": "",
      "unit_si": "",
